description:
In Elixir a module name is an atom and can be called through (`m.compare(a, b)`):

    defmodule Cmp do
      def compare(a, b), do: Kernel.compare(a, b)
    end
    def via(m, a, b), do: m.compare(a, b)
    def main(), do: dbg(via(Cmp, 1, 2))

Elixir prints :lt. The first half, a module name in value position is the atom Elixir.<Name>, is its own ticket (fz-sc8.72), split off 2026-11-07 because fz-sc8.61 needs it. This ticket keeps the second half: a remote call whose module is only known at runtime (resolved through the analysis where the value is known; a genuinely unknown module needs a runtime lookup or a loud refusal). Investigate before designing: what the concordant ticket fz-sc8.25 (one module resolution for qualified calls) changes, and how this interacts with protocols.

Needed by the Enum extremes ticket for the module-sorter form (`Enum.max(dates, Date)`). Not needed by the distiller.
